{
  "_doc": [
    "The frames the app draws, cut from the Sprout Lands packs by scripts/build-atlas.py into",
    "public/sprites/atlas.png and src/map/atlas.json. Edit this file, then run: npm run art:atlas",
    "packs: pack id -> the folder name the pack unzips to (under public/assets/sprout-lands).",
    "groups: group id -> list of sheets. A sheet is one PNG: {pack, file (path inside the pack), frames}.",
    "A frame is {name, tile: [column, row]} for one cell of the sheet's tile grid (\"tile\" on the sheet, default 16 px),",
    "or {name, rect: [x, y, w, h]} in source pixels. \"trim\": true crops the frame to its opaque pixels.",
    "A sheet with \"anim\" holds character animations: cells of anim.cell px, anim.columns per row, one row per dir,",
    "each animation starting at its row in anim.rows. Frames are named <prefix>_<anim>_<dir>_<n>, empty cells skipped,",
    "and the frame count of each <anim>_<dir> goes to atlas.json \"counts\".",
    "Frames that come out fully transparent are left out. Atlas names must be unique.",
    "copies: files copied out of the packs as they are (scale: whole-number nearest-neighbour upscale).",
    "Group titles are shown in the design library (Art, Used by the app)."
  ],
  "packs": {
    "sprites-premium": "Sprout Lands - Sprites - premium pack",
    "sprites-basic": "Sprout Lands - Sprites - Basic pack",
    "ui-premium": "Sprout Lands - UI Pack - Premium pack",
    "ui-basic": "Sprout Lands - UI Pack - Basic pack"
  },
  "atlas": {"png": "public/sprites/atlas.png", "json": "src/map/atlas.json", "width": 512, "gap": 1},
  "titles": {
    "characters": "Characters",
    "crops": "Crops",
    "ground": "Ground",
    "buildings": "Buildings",
    "decor": "Decor",
    "emotes": "UI emotes"
  },
